d2full 0015: passive_stats() skips summoning skills (a summon row, or Revive). Their passivestats are the pet's (Fight's pet set-up applies them, FUN_005c4470), but the player got them too: one point in Skeleton Mastery gave a Necromancer with Raise Skeleton +2048 max life (maxhp is 256ths there), golems added run speed, Oak Sage / Heart of Wolverine / Spirit of Barbs 100% poison resist. game.exe puts passive stats on the player only from skills with a passivestate (FUN_00646f20); none of these has one. One concern: player passives.

--- a/components/rules/skills.hpp
+++ b/components/rules/skills.hpp
@@ -711,7 +711,7 @@
 struct PassiveStat { int stat = -1, value = 0; std::string itype; };
 
